1. Why is long long safer than int for large byte counts?
So that it can prevent integer overflow.
2. Why would dividing by 1024 using only integer operands lose information?
 Because when it is dividing integers, it will discard the remainder (decimal), making it inaccurate.
3. What is the difference between changing a value's type and changing only how many decimals are displayed?
Changing a value's type will also change it in the system, but changing only how a decimal is displayed will not change the data in the system.
